Ming-3.0-tts-0.5B on LiteRT

The graphs and host files in this repository are converted from:
- inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts-0.5B (Hugging Face), revision 8d66b70a00f05ad183fa8a863b4ce609fc83cbc0, MIT License
  https://huggingface.co/inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts-0.5B
- inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts (GitHub), commit 028c1eace193e7acdb256453da89b6e9207e052b, MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2025 inclusionAI
  https://github.com/inclusionAI/Ming-3.0-tts
LICENSE is that license, unchanged.

What the conversion changed:
- The language model, flow head, aggregator and decoder were rewritten as PyTorch modules for export
  (scripts/ming_modules.py, scripts/r4_modules.py) with the same arithmetic in float32: the KV caches,
  RoPE tables and attention masks became graph inputs, the flow's 10 solver steps and classifier-free
  guidance run inside one graph, and the decoder runs 16 latents per call with a 64-position cache.
- Weights are stored as float16 (ai-edge-quantizer FLOAT_CASTING); inputs, outputs and the CPU and
  GPU FP32 arithmetic stay float32.
- lm2_epsdiv_prefill_wfp16.tflite and lm2_epsdiv_step_wfp16.tflite (the faster all-NPU placement) are
  the language model with its normalization's eps / (m * m) computed as (eps / m) / m, the same in real
  arithmetic, one signature per file (scripts/export_npu_lm.py).
- tokenizer.json is the upstream file. embed_tokens_f16.bin, istft_window.bin, stop_head.bin and
  temb_epss10.bin are tensors of the checkpoint (the last computed with its time embedder);
  tokenizer_*.txt and char_classes.bin are tables made from tokenizer.json and Python's Unicode data.
- The text normalizer and the voice-cloning path (audio encoder, CAM++ speaker model) are not converted.

android/ and scripts/ were written for this conversion. scripts/host_mirror.py and the app's Kotlin
host code follow the upstream inference code (prompt contract, tokenizer, decode loop, ISTFT).
The Android app uses LiteRT 2.2.0 (Apache License 2.0). Its NPU path needs Qualcomm's runtime
libraries, which are not part of this repository.
